# Build context exclusions for the backend image.
#
# The build context is `backend/`. Everything not needed to resolve
# dependencies and install the `app` package is excluded, which keeps the
# context small and -- more importantly -- guarantees that secrets and
# host-specific state can never end up in an image layer.

# --- Secrets: never copy a real .env into an image ---
# Configuration is injected at runtime (compose `environment:`/`env_file:`),
# so the image stays environment-agnostic and publishable.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Host virtualenv ---
# Built for Windows here; the image builds its own Linux venv from uv.lock.
.venv/

# --- Caches and build artifacts ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# --- Runtime state (recreated by ensure_runtime_directories at startup) ---
# Uploaded images and generated reports are host data, not image content;
# in containers they live on named volumes instead.
storage/
logs/
reports/

# --- Tests and developer tooling ---
# The image is a runtime artifact. Quality gates run in CI and on the host
# against the source tree, not inside the shipped image.
#
# `evaluation/` is deliberately NOT excluded: EVALUATION__ENABLED defaults to
# true and DatasetLoader reads evaluation/dataset.json (512 bytes) at request
# time, so dropping it would 500 a live endpoint. `scripts/` is likewise kept
# -- scripts/run_workers.py is the worker role's entrypoint.
tests/

# --- Documentation ---
# README.md is the one exception: pyproject.toml declares `readme = "README.md"`,
# so hatchling reads it while building the wheel and the build fails without it.
*.md
!README.md
docs/

# --- Editor / OS noise ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
